            "startSeconds": 191,
            "endSeconds": 278,
            "summary": "A 5th grade student advocating for advanced English (ELA) classes at Kennedy Middle School, explaining that she is an English language learner who wants to improve her skills to pursue her dream of becoming a pilot."
          },
          {
            "name": "Nia Seaburger",
            "startSeconds": 296,
            "endSeconds": 453,
            "summary": "A student born in China who spoke about needing advanced English coursework at Kennedy Middle School to prepare for AP classes in high school and to achieve academic success, noting that many students lack outside support."
          },
          {
            "name": "Maple",
            "startSeconds": 467,
            "endSeconds": 560,
            "summary": "A student with a high i-Ready score at the 92nd percentile nationally for 8th graders who described feeling bored and disengaged without sufficiently challenging curriculum and requested advanced ELA at Kennedy."
          },
          {
            "name": "Maya Rose",
            "startSeconds": 567,
            "endSeconds": 678,
            "summary": "A student whose parents had limited education advocated for advanced coursework at Kennedy Middle School, stating she needs excellent English skills to pursue her dream of becoming a lawyer."
          },
          {
            "name": "Greta",
            "startSeconds": 685,
            "endSeconds": 818,
            "summary": "A 5th grade Orion Mandarin Immersion student asked the board to add advanced English and challenging classes to Kennedy, noting she chose Kennedy over North Star to stay with friends but is concerned about the rigor of available coursework."
          },
          {
            "name": "Luis Velasquez",
            "startSeconds": 839,
            "endSeconds": 1023,
            "summary": "A parent and Stanford instructor argued that removing advanced ELA in the name of equity is regressive and heartbreaking, and asked the board to reinstate Advanced ELA at Kennedy for all high-performing students."
          },
          {
            "name": "Alexis Velasquez",
            "startSeconds": 1036,
            "endSeconds": 1111,
            "summary": "A 5th grade student at Orion with i-Ready scores indicating 8th grade readiness asked the board to add as many advanced classes as possible to Kennedy, including advanced ELA and science."
          },
          {
            "name": "Olbia",
            "startSeconds": 1120,
            "endSeconds": 1207,
            "summary": "A 5th grade Orion student planning to attend Kennedy asked the board to reinstate advanced ELA classes, comparing the need to the existing advanced math program and noting that students have different appetites for challenge."
          },
          {
            "name": "Megan",
            "startSeconds": 1237,
            "endSeconds": 1420,
            "summary": "A parent argued that limiting advanced coursework for some students in the name of equity is ethically dubious and ineffective, praised existing administrators Katherine Rivera and Winnie Wong, and urged the district to expand advanced ELA access across school sites."
          }
        ],
